M and Dart \"\n+                     \"(on JavaScript, their shared runtime number stays \"\n+                     \"in the host adapter). It still drops tail \"\n+                     \"flags, which makes it a good identity for \"\n+                     \"alpha-equivalence and unusable as an executable \"\n+                     \"form. This is the closest thing yin.vm has to \"\n+                     \"Unison's hash: a hash of the nameless term.\"]\n                     [:li [:strong \"The resolved tuples (implemented, no identity): \"] \"the De Bruijn form of the named datoms that both executable lowerers consume. They carry exact scalars, free names, and tail flags, and they deliberately have no hash: they are a stage value, computed and discarded, under the project's \\\"derive, don't persist\\\" rule.\"]\n                     [:li [:strong \"The stack image, \" [:code \"H\"] \" (implemented): \"] \"a linear instruction vector with \" [:code \":load-bound [depth position]\"] \" for bound variables, \" [:code \":load-free name\"] \" for free ones, and arities instead of parameter names. \" [:code \"H\"] \" hashes the descriptor and the canonical vector; binder names live in a side table outside it.\"]\n                     [:li [:strong \"The register image, \" [:code \"R\"] \" (implemented through R2): \"] \"a peer of the stack image, lowered from the same resolved tuples, never from the stack image. \" [:code \"R\"] \" hashes its own descriptor and canonical register vector, including in-band live-register sets at every continuation boundary. Neither \" [:code \"H\"] \" nor \" [:code \"R\"] \" mentions the other.\"]]\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc\nindex 331da4bb..448edee3 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc\n@@ -37,9 +37,10 @@\n    rightmost-wins, matching `yin.vm.engine/bind-params`. A bound\n    occurrence is {:bound [frame-depth position]}; a free one {:free name}.\n \