{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc | sed -n '1,260p;850,1050p;1100,1420p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/pipeline_test.cljc | sed -n '445,590p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.debruijn\n     2\t  \"Alpha-canonical de Bruijn projection of the named Universal AST\n     3\t   (docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md).\n     4\t\n     5\t   This namespace is D0-D3 of that design: the published\n     6\t   :yin.debruijn/* dimension and its hash domain, §5's canonical value\n     7\t   table with the NFC seam, §2's root framing and input validation, §3's\n     8\t   scope resolver, §4-§5's Merkle records — node hashes over the\n     9\t   dimension hash, hash-consed records with canonically spelled scalars,\n    10\t   and the root fingerprint — the settled canonical byte encoder whose\n    11\t   rules make those bytes identical on the JVM, JS, and Dart hosts, and\n    12\t   the pure d5 storage adapter over the projected records. The dao.stream\n    13\t   forward-step is D4's; it is not here.\n    14\t\n    15\t   The projection is an interpreter over plain AST datoms and never\n    16\t   executes values, primitives, streams, continuations, or effects. Its\n    17\t   input domain is a fully macro-expanded Universal AST, so an\n    18\t   unexpanded macro call site is a terminal diagnostic: an application\n    19\t   whose operator is a :lambda carrying :macro? true is unexpanded. A free\n    20\t   variable whose name matches a registry macro cannot be detected from\n    21\t   these datoms — that detection limit is inherited and documented here,\n    22\t   not enforced.\n    23\t\n    24\t   Input contract (§2): assert-only d5 datoms (only the reserved\n    25\t   :db/retract op is diagnosed; any other provenance m stays valid, and t\n    26\t   and m never enter projected identity); exactly one :yin/root true fact\n    27\t   per graph; the fact index resets at every root-frame boundary because\n    28\t   emitter tempids may restart at -16; attributes outside the :yin\n    29\t   namespace are ignored; :yin/tail? and :yin/macro-name are\n    30\t   tolerated-and-ignored emission metadata; an unknown :yin/* attribute\n    31\t   on a walked node is a diagnostic.\n    32\t\n    33\t   Scope convention (§3, the owner's settled decisions): frame depth 0 is\n    34\t   the innermost frame, position is the source parameter index with the\n    35\t   leftmost parameter at 0, frames search inner-to-outer, and positions\n    36\t   search right-to-left within a frame — duplicate parameters are\n    37\t   rightmost-wins, matching `yin.vm.engine/bind-params`. A bound\n    38\t   occurrence is {:bound [frame-depth position]}; a free one {:free name}.\n    39\t\n    40\t   Canonical limits fixed in D0 (Section 5): NFC normalisation collisions\n    41\t   are an inherited limit of the repository encoding; int64 and double\n    42\t   are disjoint classes (contract version 1), so 1 and 1.0 never merge\n    43\t   on JVM/Dart; the Dart NFC source is the unorm_dart package\n    44\t   (Unicode 16.0, owner-settled 2026-09-21) behind the one\n    45\t   host-dispatched `normalize-nfc` seam.\"\n    46\t  (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\n    47\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    48\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    49\t            #?(:cljd [\"package:unorm_dart/unorm_dart.dart\" :as unorm]))\n    50\t  #?(:cljd (:import [\"dart:typed_data\" ByteData Uint8List])))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t;; =============================================================================\n    54\t;; D0: the published dimension and its hash domain (§4, datom.md §META-PROTOCOL)\n    55\t;; =============================================================================\n    56\t\n    57\t(def contract-version\n    58\t  \"The :yin.debruijn/* contract version. Version 1 is type-preserving:\n    59\t   :int64 and :double are disjoint, and integral doubles are never\n    60\t   folded into :int64.\"\n    61\t  1)\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(def canonical-value-table\n    65\t  \"§5's canonical value table as data: the classes a projected scalar may\n    66\t   carry and the rule that fixes each one's encoding. Bounds are symbolic\n    67\t   (:signed-int64) and host-neutral, so the table — and therefore\n    68\t   the descriptor that embeds it — prints identically on every host;\n    69\t   `canonical-class` below pins the numbers. D3's encoder consumes this\n    70\t   table; D0 consumes it for validation.\"\n    71\t  {:classes [:nil :bool :int64 :double :string :bytes :keyword :symbol\n    72\t             :map :set :vector :list],\n    73\t   :framing {:slots :tagged-and-length-delimited},\n    74\t   :nil {:encoding :own-tag},\n    75\t   :bool {:bytes {false \"00\", true \"01\"}},\n    76\t   :int64 {:domain :signed-int64, :endianness :little},\n    77\t   :double {:format :ieee-754,\n    78\t            :nan :one-quiet-nan,\n    79\t            :signed-zero :distinct,\n    80\t            :integral-double-folding false},\n    81\t   :string {:encoding :utf-8, :normalization :nfc, :framing :length-prefixed},\n    82\t   :bytes {:framing :length-prefixed},\n    83\t   :keyword {:components [:namespace :name], :encoding :nfc-utf-8},\n    84\t   :symbol {:components [:namespace :name], :encoding :nfc-utf-8},\n    85\t   :map {:key-order :canonical-encoded-bytes},\n    86\t   :set {:element-order :canonical-encoded-bytes},\n    87\t   ;; vectors and lists are distinct classes: `vector?` observes the\n    88\t   ;; difference, so one class would be an undeclared semantic collision\n    89\t   :vector {:order :positional},\n    90\t   :list {:order :positional},\n    91\t   :numbers {:out-of-domain [:bigint :ratio :char :other-numeric]},\n    92\t   :limits [:nfc-normalization-collisions]})\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t(def dimension-slots\n    96\t  \"The projected d5 semantic slots in §4's declared order, each as\n    97\t   [slot-name slot-type slot-role]. Roles: :scalar enters node identity;\n    98\t   :child is an ordered child ref carrying child hashes; :marker is\n    99\t   storage/index (§5 excludes :yin.debruijn/hash and :yin.debruijn/root\n   100\t   from every node hash). :yin.debruijn/operands is the one\n   101\t   ordered-vector slot.\"\n   102\t  [[:yin.debruijn/hash :hash :marker]\n   103\t   [:yin.debruijn/type :keyword :scalar]\n   104\t   [:yin.debruijn/arity :int64 :scalar]\n   105\t   [:yin.debruijn/bound [:tuple :int64 :int64] :scalar]\n   106\t   [:yin.debruijn/free :symbol :scalar]\n   107\t   [:yin.debruijn/value :canonical :scalar]\n   108\t   [:yin.debruijn/op :keyword :scalar]\n   109\t   [:yin.debruijn/key :symbol :scalar]\n   110\t   [:yin.debruijn/prefix :string :scalar]\n   111\t   [:yin.debruijn/buffer :int64 :scalar]\n   112\t   [:yin.debruijn/parked-id :keyword :scalar]\n   113\t   [:yin.debruijn/macro? :bool :scalar]\n   114\t   [:yin.debruijn/body :ref :child]\n   115\t   [:yin.debruijn/operator :ref :child]\n   116\t   [:yin.debruijn/operands [:ordered-vector :ref] :child]\n   117\t   [:yin.debruijn/test :ref :child]\n   118\t   [:yin.debruijn/consequent :ref :child]\n   119\t   [:yin.debruijn/alternate :ref :child]\n   120\t   [:yin.debruijn/target :ref :child]\n   121\t   [:yin.debruijn/val-node :ref :child]\n   122\t   [:yin.debruijn/source :ref :child]\n   123\t   [:yin.debruijn/root :bool :marker]])\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\t(def descriptor\n   127\t  \"The :yin.debruijn/* dimension published per datom.md's meta-protocol:\n   128\t   the small d3 subgraph [s a v] declaring arity, ordered slots, the\n   129\t   canonical encoding rule parameterized by the slot types, and the\n   130\t   anchor morphisms. The content hash of this subgraph — `dimension-hash`\n   131\t   below — IS the dimension's identity and the projection's hash domain\n   132\t   separator: not an ad hoc text string.\"\n   133\t  [[:yin.debruijn/dimension :dim/contract-version contract-version]\n   134\t   [:yin.debruijn/dimension :dim/arity 22]\n   135\t   [:yin.debruijn/dimension :dim/slots dimension-slots]\n   136\t   [:yin.debruijn/dimension\n   137\t    :dim/encoding\n   138\t    {:hash :sha256,\n   139\t     :node-hash \"SHA-256(dimension-hash || encode(tag-specific-slots-in-descriptor-order))\",\n   140\t     :slot-order :descriptor,\n   141\t     :tag-specific-slots-only true,\n   142\t     :hash-excluded-slots [:yin.debruijn/hash :yin.debruijn/root],\n   143\t     :child-order :declared,\n   144\t     :values canonical-value-table}]\n   145\t   [:yin.debruijn/dimension\n   146\t    :dim/projection-to\n   147\t    [[:d1 \"content-addressing floor: every projected node reduces to its node hash\"]\n   148\t     [:d3 \"semantic floor: each projected record is (h, :yin.debruijn/<slot>, v)\"]]]\n   149\t   [:yin.debruijn/dimension\n   150\t    :dim/lift-from\n   151\t    [[:d5 \"the named :yin/* Universal AST datoms (yin.vm/ast->datoms-with-root)\"\n   152\t      \"yin.vm.debruijn/project-datoms is the lift\"]]]])\n   153\t\n   154\t\n   155\t;; dimension-hash is minted below, beside the canonical encoder: §5's\n   156\t;; domain separator is the descriptor encoded through the settled encoder\n   157\t;; and hashed, and the encoder's definitions intervene between the two.\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\t;; =============================================================================\n   161\t;; D0: the canonical value table as validation, and the NFC seam (§5)\n   162\t;; =============================================================================\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn- bytes-like?\n   165\t  [v]\n   166\t  #?(:clj (bytes? v)\n   167\t     :cljs (instance? js/Uint8Array v)\n   168\t     :cljd (instance? Uint8List v)))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t#?(:cljs\n   172\t   (defn- js-number-class\n   173\t     \"The JS adapter's classification of a JS number, whose one type cannot\n   174\t      tell 1 from 1.0 (a host limit that stays here, never in the universal\n   175\t      projection): a safe integer is :int64; NaN, the infinities, -0.0, and\n   176\t      non-integral values are :double; an unsafe integral is nil, a\n   177\t      diagnostic rather than a silently misclaimed int64.\"\n   178\t     [v]\n   179\t     (cond\n   180\t       (not= v v) :double\n   181\t       (or (= js/Infinity v) (= js/-Infinity v)) :double\n   182\t       (and (zero? v) (= js/-Infinity (/ 1.0 v))) :double\n   183\t       (not= v (js/Math.floor v)) :double\n   184\t       (<= -9007199254740991 v 9007199254740991) :int64\n   185\t       :else nil)))\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\t#?(:cljs\n   189\t   (defn- has-integral-number?\n   190\t     \"True when v is, or nests, a JS number classified :int64: a value the\n   191\t      wire may have carried as a double, whose class this host cannot\n   192\t      recover.\"\n   193\t     [v]\n   194\t     (cond\n   195\t       (number? v) (= :int64 (js-number-class v))\n   196\t       (map? v) (some (fn [[k x]]\n   197\t                        (or (has-integral-number? k)\n   198\t                            (has-integral-number? x)))\n   199\t                      v)\n   200\t       (coll? v) (some has-integral-number? v)\n   201\t       :else false)))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t#?(:cljs\n   205\t   (defn- refuse-unrecoverable-integral!\n   206\t     \"Throw :unsupported-value when record's value nests a JS number whose\n   207\t      wire class (int64 or integral double) this host cannot recover.\"\n   208\t     [record h e]\n   209\t     (when (has-integral-number? (:yin.debruijn/value record))\n   210\t       (throw (ex-info \"Integral number of unrecoverable class\"\n   211\t                       {:rule :unsupported-value, :hash h, :entity e})))))\n   212\t\n   213\t\n   214\t(defn- numeric-class\n   215\t  \"Classify a number under the type-preserving numeric rule (contract\n   216\t   version 1): int64 and double are disjoint. Host integers (Long on the\n   217\t   JVM, Dart int) are :int64 and every floating-point value is :double,\n   218\t   integral or not; bigints, ratios, and friends classify nil. Only the\n   219\t   :cljs adapter, where 1 and 1.0 are one number, classifies by value.\"\n   220\t  [v]\n   221\t  #?(:clj (cond\n   222\t            (int? v) :int64\n   223\t            (float? v) :double\n   224\t            :else nil)\n   225\t     :cljs (js-number-class v)\n   226\t     :cljd (if (int? v) :int64 :double)))\n   227\t\n   228\t\n   229\t(defn- code-unit-at\n   230\t  [s i]\n   231\t  #?(:clj (int (.charAt ^String s i))\n   232\t     :cljs (.charCodeAt s i)\n   233\t     :cljd (.codeUnitAt s i)))\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\t(defn- well-formed-utf16?\n   237\t  \"True when every surrogate in `s` is paired — the precondition for the\n   238\t   hosts' UTF-8 encoders to agree. An unpaired surrogate reaches storage\n   239\t   as itself on some hosts and as the replacement character on others,\n   240\t   so byte identity is unmakeable there: such a string classifies\n   241\t   unsupported, in a value or in an ident's parts alike.\"\n   242\t  [s]\n   243\t  (let [n (count s)]\n   244\t    (loop [i 0]\n   245\t      (if (>= i n)\n   246\t        true\n   247\t        (let [c (code-unit-at s i)]\n   248\t          (cond\n   249\t            (<= 0xDC00 c 0xDFFF) false\n   250\t            (<= 0xD800 c 0xDBFF) (if (and (< (inc i) n)\n   251\t                                          (<= 0xDC00 (code-unit-at s (inc i)) 0xDFFF))\n   252\t                                   (recur (+ i 2))\n   253\t                                   false)\n   254\t            :else (recur (inc i))))))))\n   255\t\n   256\t\n   257\t(defn- ident-parts-ok?\n   258\t  \"An identifier classifies only when its namespace and name are both\n   259\t   well-formed UTF-16: ident parts are strings under NFC.\"\n   260\t  [x]\n   850\t                                   2))]\n   851\t             (apply str (map #(byte-at (if (< % 4) lo hi) (mod % 4)) (range 8))))\n   852\t     :default (let [n (long v)]\n   853\t                (apply str (map #(to-hex (bit-and (unsigned-bit-shift-right n (* % 8)) 0xff) 2)\n   854\t                                (range 8))))))\n   855\t\n   856\t\n   857\t(defn- double-le-hex\n   858\t  \"The settled :double byte rule: the IEEE-754 bits, little-endian, with\n   859\t   every NaN the one quiet encoding 7ff8000000000000 regardless of the\n   860\t   payload a host happens to hold. :clj reads the bits through\n   861\t   doubleToLongBits, :cljs through a DataView store with littleEndian\n   862\t   explicitly true, :cljd through a big-endian ByteData store read in\n   863\t   reverse — the endianness is stated, never the platform's default.\"\n   864\t  [v]\n   865\t  (if (not= v v)\n   866\t    \"000000000000f87f\"\n   867\t    #?(:clj (int64-le-hex (Double/doubleToLongBits (double v)))\n   868\t       :cljs (let [view (js/DataView. (js/ArrayBuffer. 8))]\n   869\t               (.setFloat64 view 0 v true)\n   870\t               (apply str (map #(to-hex (.getUint8 view %) 2) (range 8))))\n   871\t       :cljd (let [bd (ByteData. 8)]\n   872\t               (.setFloat64 bd 0 v)\n   873\t               (apply str (map #(to-hex (.getUint8 bd %) 2) (range 7 -1 -1)))))))\n   874\t\n   875\t\n   876\t(defn- ident-content\n   877\t  \"§5 keywords and symbols encode namespace and name separately, each\n   878\t   through the NFC seam — the value table declares :nfc-utf-8 for both\n   879\t   parts; an absent namespace has nil's own framing, never an empty\n   880\t   string's.\"\n   881\t  [x]\n   882\t  (str (if-let [ns (namespace x)]\n   883\t         (framed :string (normalize-nfc ns))\n   884\t         (framed :nil \"\"))\n   885\t       (framed :string (normalize-nfc (name x)))))\n   886\t\n   887\t\n   888\t(defn encode-value\n   889\t  \"Encode one canonical-domain value under its value-table class: the\n   890\t   full tagged, length-delimited part, under the settled D3 byte rules —\n   891\t   int64 little-endian two's complement for integers, IEEE-754 bits with\n   892\t   one quiet-NaN encoding for doubles (1 and 1.0 stay distinct), UTF-8 byte\n   893\t   lengths, NFC strings and ident parts. Maps and sets sort by their encoded\n   894\t   parts, the Section 5 order rule; vectors and lists are the distinct classes\n   895\t   the D0 ruling split. An out-of-domain value is a diagnostic.\"\n   896\t  [v]\n   897\t  (let [class (canonical-class v)]\n   898\t    (case class\n   899\t      :nil (framed :nil \"\")\n   900\t      :bool (framed :bool (if v \"01\" \"00\"))\n   901\t      :int64 (framed :int64 (int64-le-hex v))\n   902\t      :double (framed :double (double-le-hex v))\n   903\t      :string (framed :string (normalize-nfc v))\n   904\t      :bytes (framed :bytes (apply str (map #(to-hex (bit-and % 0xff) 2) v)))\n   905\t      :keyword (framed :keyword (ident-content v))\n   906\t      :symbol (framed :symbol (ident-content v))\n   907\t      :map (let [entries (sort (map (fn [[k x]]\n   908\t                                      [(encode-value k) (encode-value x)])\n   909\t                                    v))]\n   910\t             (when (some (fn [[a b]] (= (first a) (first b)))\n   911\t                         (partition 2 1 entries))\n   912\t               (throw (ex-info \"Map keys collide in canonical encoding\"\n   913\t                               {:rule :unsupported-value, :value v})))\n   914\t             (framed :map (apply str (mapcat identity entries))))\n   915\t      :set (let [elements (sort (map encode-value v))]\n   916\t             (when (some (fn [[a b]] (= a b)) (partition 2 1 elements))\n   917\t               (throw (ex-info \"Set elements collide in canonical encoding\"\n   918\t                               {:rule :unsupported-value, :value v})))\n   919\t             (framed :set (apply str elements)))\n   920\t      :vector (framed :vector (apply str (map encode-value v)))\n   921\t      :list (framed :list (apply str (map encode-value v)))\n   922\t      (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported value in Merkle encoding\"\n   923\t                      {:rule :unsupported-value, :value v})))))\n   924\t\n   925\t\n   926\t(defn- encode-typed\n   927\t  \"Encode one descriptor slot's value under its declared type:\n   928\t   :canonical is polymorphic, the compound types frame their parts, and\n   929\t   a declared scalar type encodes by its (already validated) value\n   930\t   class.\"\n   931\t  [type v]\n   932\t  (cond\n   933\t    (= :canonical type) (encode-value v)\n   934\t    (vector? type) (if (= :tuple (first type))\n   935\t                     (framed :tuple (apply str (map encode-typed (rest type) v)))\n   936\t                     (framed :ordered-vector\n   937\t                             (str (framed :int64 (int64-le-hex (count v)))\n   938\t                                  (apply str (map #(encode-typed :ref %) v)))))\n   939\t    (or (= :ref type) (= :hash type)) (framed :ref v)\n   940\t    :else (encode-value v)))\n   941\t\n   942\t\n   943\t(def dimension-hash\n   944\t  \"The published hash domain separator (§4): the descriptor data encoded\n   945\t   through the settled canonical encoder and hashed, per datom.md's 'the\n   946\t   content hash of this subgraph IS the dimension's identity'. D0-D2\n   947\t   minted a transitional dao.jing digest; D3 re-pins it here over the\n   948\t   settled byte rules. The descriptor content is unchanged — only the\n   949\t   digest's derivation moved to the canonical encoder, so the separator\n   950\t   now separates this dimension from every other by the same bytes every\n   951\t   node hash uses.\"\n   952\t  (jing/sha256 (encode-value descriptor)))\n   953\t\n   954\t\n   955\t(defn canonical-value\n   956\t  \"A record's stored scalar is its canonical spelling (the carried D3\n   957\t   obligation): the long form for integers and the double form for\n   958\t   doubles, so 1 and 1.0 hold distinct record contents on JVM/Dart; the\n   959\t   NFC form for strings and ident parts, and the same recursively inside\n   960\t   collections. One content address, one record content: equal fingerprints\n   961\t   imply equal :records maps.\n   962\t   Canonicalizing a map whose keys merge (for example, two string keys\n   963\t   with one NFC form) is a key collision, diagnosed rather than letting\n   964\t   iteration order decide which entry survives; a set whose elements\n   965\t   merge (such as two distinct spellings of one NFC string) is diagnosed\n   966\t   the same way, because the merge changes its count, not just a scalar's\n   967\t   spelling.\"\n   968\t  [v]\n   969\t  (let [class (canonical-class v)]\n   970\t    (case class\n   971\t      :nil v\n   972\t      :bool v\n   973\t      :int64 (long v)\n   974\t      :double (double v)\n   975\t      :string (normalize-nfc v)\n   976\t      :bytes v\n   977\t      :keyword (if-let [ns (namespace v)]\n   978\t                 (keyword (normalize-nfc ns) (normalize-nfc (name v)))\n   979\t                 (keyword (normalize-nfc (name v))))\n   980\t      :symbol (if-let [ns (namespace v)]\n   981\t                (symbol (normalize-nfc ns) (normalize-nfc (name v)))\n   982\t                (symbol (normalize-nfc (name v))))\n   983\t      :map (let [canonical (into {}\n   984\t                                 (map (fn [[k x]]\n   985\t                                        [(canonical-value k) (canonical-value x)]))\n   986\t                                 v)]\n   987\t             (if (< (count canonical) (count v))\n   988\t               (throw (ex-info \"Canonicalizing a map merges distinct keys\"\n   989\t                               {:rule :unsupported-value, :value v}))\n   990\t               canonical))\n   991\t      :set (let [canonical (into (empty v) (map canonical-value) v)]\n   992\t             (if (< (count canonical) (count v))\n   993\t               (throw (ex-info \"Canonicalizing a set merges distinct elements\"\n   994\t                               {:rule :unsupported-value, :value v}))\n   995\t               canonical))\n   996\t      :vector (mapv canonical-value v)\n   997\t      :list (apply list (map canonical-value v))\n   998\t      v)))\n   999\t\n  1000\t\n  1001\t(defn- node-hash\n  1002\t  \"§5: hash(node) = SHA-256(dimension-hash || encode(tag-specific-slots-\n  1003\t   in-descriptor-order)). The preimage is the dimension hash's hex\n  1004\t   followed by the framed slots under the settled byte rules; the shape —\n  1005\t   descriptor order, tags, byte-count length delimiters, ordered child\n  1006\t   hashes — is what D2 fixed and D3 settled. Markers are never among the\n  1007\t   encodings: only present, non-marker slots reach here.\"\n  1008\t  [encodings]\n  1009\t  (jing/sha256 (apply str dimension-hash encodings)))\n  1010\t\n  1011\t\n  1012\t;; =============================================================================\n  1013\t;; D2: hash-consing and the projected records (§4)\n  1014\t;; =============================================================================\n  1015\t\n  1016\t(defn- slot-encodings\n  1017\t  \"The descriptor-order encodings of one record's present, non-marker\n  1018\t   slots — with the dimension hash, the only input to a node hash.\n  1019\t   Children already carry child hashes, so this is total over a record\n  1020\t   and serves both the mint and the storage reader's content check.\"\n  1021\t  [record]\n  1022\t  (for [[slot type role] dimension-slots\n  1023\t        :when (and (not= :marker role) (contains? record slot))]\n  1024\t    (encode-typed type (get record slot))))\n  1025\t\n  1026\t\n  1027\t(defn- mint-record\n  1028\t  \"Hash-cons one resolved node (§4-§5) whose children are already\n  1029\t   minted, their hashes in `child-hashes` ({slot h}, an ordered vector\n  1030\t   under :yin.debruijn/operands): the node hash over the dimension hash\n  1031\t   and the node's tag-specific slots in descriptor order, then the record\n  1032\t   — the node with child slots carrying child hashes, scalars in their\n  1033\t   canonical spellings, and :yin.debruijn/hash added. Returns [h acc']\n  1034\t   over {:hashcons preimage->h, :records h->record, :mints n}; :mints\n  1035\t   counts every call, the walk's instrumentation seam. The consing memo\n  1036\t   is keyed on the node's preimage — the concatenated slot encodings —\n  1037\t   never on Clojure =, which merges a list literal with a vector literal\n  1038\t   and the signed zeros; a preimage hit implies the identical hash and,\n  1039\t   records carrying canonical spellings, the identical record. The memo\n  1040\t   stays an optimisation only: identity is the hash either way, so\n  1041\t   traversal order never enters it.\"\n  1042\t  [node child-hashes acc]\n  1043\t  (let [acc (update acc :mints inc)\n  1044\t        record (reduce (fn [r [slot _type role]]\n  1045\t                         (cond\n  1046\t                           (or (= :marker role) (not (contains? node slot))) r\n  1047\t                           (= :child role) (assoc r slot (get child-hashes slot))\n  1048\t                           ;; the carried D3 obligation: a record's stored\n  1049\t                           ;; scalar is its canonical spelling, so equal\n  1050\t                           ;; fingerprints imply equal records\n  1100\t   ex-info carrying :rule (and, where the walk has descended, :entity\n  1101\t   and :path). For a stream carrying several adjacent graphs, frame it\n  1102\t   first with `frame-datoms` and project each frame — the per-frame fact\n  1103\t   index resets there.\"\n  1104\t  [datoms]\n  1105\t  (dissoc (project-datoms-counted datoms) :mints))\n  1106\t\n  1107\t\n  1108\t;; =============================================================================\n  1109\t;; D2: the d5 storage adapter (§4)\n  1110\t;; =============================================================================\n  1111\t\n  1112\t(defn projected->datoms\n  1113\t  \"The d5 storage adapter's write half (§4): one projection's records as\n  1114\t   d5 datoms [e a v t m]. Entities are local handles minted from\n  1115\t   dao.datom's first-user-id in a deterministic root-down, descriptor\n  1116\t   slot order walk — handles, ordinals, and row count are storage layout\n  1117\t   only, never identity. Each entity carries :yin.debruijn/hash h; child\n  1118\t   slots carry child hashes; :yin.debruijn/operands is one ordered\n  1119\t   vector datom, never cardinality-many; and the root entity is\n  1120\t   explicitly marked :yin.debruijn/root true — the root-hash marker, its\n  1121\t   :yin.debruijn/hash being the fingerprint. t 0 and the assert op are\n  1122\t   the adapter's fixed provenance, mirroring the named emitter's\n  1123\t   defaults.\"\n  1124\t  [{:keys [fingerprint records]}]\n  1125\t  (let [t 0\n  1126\t        m datom/default-op\n  1127\t        out (atom [])\n  1128\t        emitted (atom #{})\n  1129\t        next-eid (atom (dec datom/first-user-id))\n  1130\t        emit! (fn [e a v] (swap! out conj [e a v t m]))\n  1131\t        walk (fn walk\n  1132\t               [h]\n  1133\t               ;; one entity per hash: a record reachable by several paths\n  1134\t               ;; is emitted once, and the slot datoms already pointing at\n  1135\t               ;; its hash are the sharing\n  1136\t               (when-not (contains? @emitted h)\n  1137\t                 (let [e (swap! next-eid inc)\n  1138\t                       ;; the records came from the projection itself, so a\n  1139\t                       ;; missing one is a projection defect, never input:\n  1140\t                       ;; its rule is one `exception-diagnostic` classifies\n  1141\t                       ;; :internal-error\n  1142\t                       record (or (get records h)\n  1143\t                                  (throw (ex-info\n  1144\t                                           \"Projected record set does not contain a child hash\"\n  1145\t                                           {:rule :missing-record, :hash h})))]\n  1146\t                   (swap! emitted conj h)\n  1147\t                   (emit! e :yin.debruijn/hash h)\n  1148\t                   (doseq [[slot type role] dimension-slots\n  1149\t                           :when (and (not= :marker role) (contains? record slot))]\n  1150\t                     (let [v (get record slot)]\n  1151\t                       (emit! e slot v)\n  1152\t                       (when (= :child role)\n  1153\t                         (if (and (vector? type) (= :ordered-vector (first type)))\n  1154\t                           (doseq [child v] (walk child))\n  1155\t                           (walk v)))))\n  1156\t                   (when (= h fingerprint)\n  1157\t                     (emit! e :yin.debruijn/root true)))))]\n  1158\t    (walk fingerprint)\n  1159\t    @out))\n  1160\t\n  1161\t\n  1162\t(def ^:private record-attributes\n  1163\t  \"Every attribute a projected record entity may carry: the declared\n  1164\t   dimension slots, markers included.\"\n  1165\t  (into #{} (map first) dimension-slots))\n  1166\t\n  1167\t\n  1168\t(defn- slot-shape-ok?\n  1169\t  \"Whether `v` fits the descriptor `type` on a projected record: the\n  1170\t   deterministic gate the storage reader hashes behind, so a wrongly\n  1171\t   typed slot — :yin.debruijn/bound 5, a numeric child ref — diagnoses\n  1172\t   :unsupported-value instead of reaching host arithmetic inside the\n  1173\t   hash recomputation.\"\n  1174\t  [type v]\n  1175\t  (cond\n  1176\t    (= :canonical type) (canonical-value? v)\n  1177\t    (= :keyword type) (keyword? v)\n  1178\t    (= :symbol type) (symbol? v)\n  1179\t    (= :string type) (string? v)\n  1180\t    (= :bool type) (or (true? v) (false? v))\n  1181\t    (= :int64 type) (and (number? v) (= :int64 (numeric-class v)))\n  1182\t    (or (= :ref type) (= :hash type)) (and (string? v)\n  1183\t                                           (re-matches #\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\" v))\n  1184\t    (and (vector? type) (= :tuple (first type)))\n  1185\t    (and (vector? v)\n  1186\t         (= (count v) (count (rest type)))\n  1187\t         (every? true? (map slot-shape-ok? (rest type) v)))\n  1188\t    (vector? type) (and (vector? v) (every? #(slot-shape-ok? :ref %) v))\n  1189\t    :else false))\n  1190\t\n  1191\t\n  1192\t(defn- projected-slots-of\n  1193\t  \"The projected slots one §2 grammar attribute becomes (§4): the binder\n  1194\t   :yin/params becomes :arity, an occurrence's :yin/name becomes one of\n  1195\t   :bound or :free, and every other attribute keeps its name under\n  1196\t   :yin.debruijn.\"\n  1197\t  [attr]\n  1198\t  (case attr\n  1199\t    :yin/params [:yin.debruijn/arity]\n  1200\t    :yin/name [:yin.debruijn/bound :yin.debruijn/free]\n  1201\t    [(keyword \"yin.debruijn\" (name attr))]))\n  1202\t\n  1203\t\n  1204\t(def ^:private record-slots\n  1205\t  \"Per node type, every slot its projected record may carry besides\n  1206\t   :yin.debruijn/hash — derived from `node-grammar`, so the reader's\n  1207\t   grammar and the walk's are one table. The preimage frames slots by\n  1208\t   type tag, not name, so this check is what keeps a slot renamed within\n  1209\t   one type (:free to :key on a :variable, :arity to :buffer) from\n  1210\t   passing under a valid address.\"\n  1211\t  (into {}\n  1212\t        (map (fn [[tag {:keys [scalars children]}]]\n  1213\t               [tag (into #{:yin.debruijn/type}\n  1214\t                          (mapcat (comp projected-slots-of first))\n  1215\t                          (concat scalars children))]))\n  1216\t        node-grammar))\n  1217\t\n  1218\t\n  1219\t(def ^:private optional-record-slots\n  1220\t  \"The record slots a writer may leave absent: :macro? (only a true one\n  1221\t   is written) and :bound/:free, of which a :variable carries exactly\n  1222\t   one.\"\n  1223\t  #{:yin.debruijn/macro? :yin.debruijn/bound :yin.debruijn/free})\n  1224\t\n  1225\t\n  1226\t(defn- canonical-spelling?\n  1227\t  \"Whether `v` is already its own canonical spelling — the form\n  1228\t   `canonical-value` gives every stored scalar. Exact, never =: Dart's\n  1229\t   1 == 1.0 and Clojure's = across a set's members would pass a stored\n  1230\t   1.0 whose address is 1's, and the reader would hand back a record no\n  1231\t   writer produces. A JS number carries one spelling per value, so every\n  1232\t   in-domain number is canonical there.\"\n  1233\t  [v]\n  1234\t  (case (canonical-class v)\n  1235\t    (:nil :bool :bytes) true\n  1236\t    :int64 #?(:cljs true :default (int? v))\n  1237\t    ;; :cljd first: the ClojureDart host pass also reads :clj\n  1238\t    :double #?(:cljd true :clj (instance? Double v) :cljs true)\n  1239\t    :string (= v (normalize-nfc v))\n  1240\t    (:keyword :symbol) (and (or (nil? (namespace v))\n  1241\t                                (= (namespace v) (normalize-nfc (namespace v))))\n  1242\t                            (= (name v) (normalize-nfc (name v))))\n  1243\t    :map (every? (fn [[k x]] (and (canonical-spelling? k) (canonical-spelling? x))) v)\n  1244\t    (:set :vector :list) (every? canonical-spelling? v)\n  1245\t    false))\n  1246\t\n  1247\t\n  1248\t(defn- check-record\n  1249\t  \"The reader's record gate, after every slot fits its declared shape:\n  1250\t   the record's type is a grammar type, it carries exactly its type's\n  1251\t   slots (a :variable exactly one of :bound/:free, a :macro? only when\n  1252\t   true), and every scalar is its canonical spelling. Everything here is\n  1253\t   what the writer already guarantees, so no minted hash moves.\"\n  1254\t  [record e]\n  1255\t  (let [tag (get record :yin.debruijn/type)\n  1256\t        allowed (or (get record-slots tag)\n  1257\t                    (throw (ex-info \"Projected record has an unknown node type\"\n  1258\t                                    {:rule :unknown-node-type, :type tag, :entity e})))\n  1259\t        present (disj (set (keys record)) :yin.debruijn/hash)]\n  1260\t    (doseq [slot present]\n  1261\t      (when-not (contains? allowed slot)\n  1262\t        (throw (ex-info \"Projected slot is outside its node type's grammar row\"\n  1263\t                        {:rule :unknown-attribute,\n  1264\t                         :attribute slot,\n  1265\t                         :type tag,\n  1266\t                         :entity e}))))\n  1267\t    (doseq [slot allowed]\n  1268\t      (when-not (or (contains? present slot)\n  1269\t                    (contains? optional-record-slots slot))\n  1270\t        (throw (ex-info \"Projected record lacks a required slot\"\n  1271\t                        {:rule :missing-slot, :slot slot, :type tag, :entity e}))))\n  1272\t    (when (and (= :variable tag)\n  1273\t               (not= 1 (count (filter #(contains? present %)\n  1274\t                                      [:yin.debruijn/bound :yin.debruijn/free]))))\n  1275\t      (throw (ex-info \"A projected :variable carries exactly one of :bound and :free\"\n  1276\t                      {:rule :missing-slot,\n  1277\t                       :slot [:yin.debruijn/bound :yin.debruijn/free],\n  1278\t                       :type tag,\n  1279\t                       :entity e})))\n  1280\t    (doseq [[slot _type role] dimension-slots\n  1281\t            :when (and (= :scalar role) (contains? record slot))]\n  1282\t      (let [v (get record slot)]\n  1283\t        (when-not (and (canonical-spelling? v)\n  1284\t                       ;; the writer spells a false :macro? by its absence\n  1285\t                       (not (and (= :yin.debruijn/macro? slot) (false? v))))\n  1286\t          (throw (ex-info \"Projected scalar is not its canonical spelling\"\n  1287\t                          {:rule :noncanonical-value,\n  1288\t                           :slot slot,\n  1289\t                           :value v,\n  1290\t                           :entity e})))))))\n  1291\t\n  1292\t\n  1293\t(defn datoms->projected\n  1294\t  \"The d5 storage adapter's read half (§4): projected datoms back to\n  1295\t   {:fingerprint h, :records {h record}} — the inverse of\n  1296\t   `projected->datoms` over the record set (the resolved :root graph is\n  1297\t   the named side's, never rebuilt here). Every entity must carry its\n  1298\t   :yin.debruijn/hash; exactly one entity is the :yin.debruijn/root\n  1299\t   marker and its hash is the fingerprint; every slot must fit its\n  1300\t   declared shape BEFORE its hash is recomputed — a wrongly typed slot\n  1301\t   diagnoses :unsupported-value, never a host exception; each record must\n  1302\t   then be one its writer can produce — its type's grammar slots only\n  1303\t   (:unknown-node-type, :unknown-attribute, :missing-slot), every scalar\n  1304\t   in its canonical spelling (:noncanonical-value) — because the\n  1305\t   preimage frames slots by type tag, not name, and equal encodings do\n  1306\t   not mean equal spellings; child refs must resolve to records;\n  1307\t   :yin.debruijn/operands must be one vector of hashes. Each record is\n  1308\t   re-hashed and a disagreement is a\n  1309\t   :hash-mismatch diagnostic — content addressing is verified at this\n  1310\t   boundary, never trusted. t, m, and other namespaces are layout,\n  1311\t   ignored.\"\n  1312\t  [datoms]\n  1313\t  (let [datoms (vec datoms)\n  1314\t        index (index-frame \"yin.debruijn\" datoms)\n  1315\t        markers (into []\n  1316\t                      (comp (filter #(= :yin.debruijn/root (nth % 1)))\n  1317\t                            (filter #(true? (nth % 2)))\n  1318\t                            (map first))\n  1319\t                      datoms)\n  1320\t        _ (when-not (= 1 (count markers))\n  1321\t            (throw (ex-info \"Projected datoms have not exactly one root marker\"\n  1322\t                            (if (zero? (count markers))\n  1323\t                              {:rule :missing-root}\n  1324\t                              {:rule :multiple-roots, :roots markers}))))\n  1325\t        root-e (first markers)\n  1326\t        records (reduce-kv (fn [recs e facts]\n  1327\t                             (let [h (or (when (contains? facts :yin.debruijn/hash)\n  1328\t                                           (get facts :yin.debruijn/hash))\n  1329\t                                         (throw (ex-info\n  1330\t                                                  \"Projected entity carries no :yin.debruijn/hash\"\n  1331\t                                                  {:rule :missing-hash, :entity e})))\n  1332\t                                   record (dissoc facts :yin.debruijn/root)]\n  1333\t                               (doseq [a (keys record)]\n  1334\t                                 (when-not (contains? record-attributes a)\n  1335\t                                   (throw (ex-info\n  1336\t                                            \"Unknown :yin.debruijn/* attribute on a projected record\"\n  1337\t                                            {:rule :unknown-attribute,\n  1338\t                                             :attribute a,\n  1339\t                                             :entity e}))))\n  1340\t                               (when-not (and (string? h)\n  1341\t                                              (re-matches #\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\" h))\n  1342\t                                 (throw (ex-info \"Projected hash is not 64 lowercase hex\"\n  1343\t                                                 {:rule :malformed-hash,\n  1344\t                                                  :hash h,\n  1345\t                                                  :entity e})))\n  1346\t                               (doseq [[slot type role] dimension-slots\n  1347\t                                       :when (and (not= :marker role)\n  1348\t                                                  (contains? record slot))]\n  1349\t                                 (when-not (slot-shape-ok? type (get record slot))\n  1350\t                                   (throw (ex-info\n  1351\t                                            \"Projected slot value does not fit its declared type\"\n  1352\t                                            {:rule :unsupported-value,\n  1353\t                                             :slot slot,\n  1354\t                                             :value (get record slot),\n  1355\t                                             :entity e}))))\n  1356\t                               (check-record record e)\n  1357\t                               (if (contains? recs h)\n  1358\t                                 (throw (ex-info\n  1359\t                                          \"Two entities claim one projected hash\"\n  1360\t                                          {:rule :duplicate-fact,\n  1361\t                                           :attribute :yin.debruijn/hash,\n  1362\t                                           :entity e}))\n  1363\t                                 (do (when-not (= h (node-hash (slot-encodings record)))\n  1364\t                                       ;; a JS number cannot say whether it\n  1365\t                                       ;; was an int64 or an integral double\n  1366\t                                       ;; on the wire: refuse, not mismatch\n  1367\t                                       #?(:cljs\n  1368\t                                          (refuse-unrecoverable-integral!\n  1369\t                                            record h e))\n  1370\t                                       (throw (ex-info\n  1371\t                                                \"Projected record does not hash to its address\"\n  1372\t                                                {:rule :hash-mismatch,\n  1373\t                                                 :hash h,\n  1374\t                                                 :entity e})))\n  1375\t                                     (assoc recs h record)))))\n  1376\t                           {}\n  1377\t                           index)\n  1378\t        fingerprint (get-in index [root-e :yin.debruijn/hash])]\n  1379\t    (doseq [[h record] records\n  1380\t            [slot type role] dimension-slots\n  1381\t            :when (and (= :child role) (contains? record slot))]\n  1382\t      (let [refs (if (and (vector? type) (= :ordered-vector (first type)))\n  1383\t                   (let [v (get record slot)]\n  1384\t                     (when-not (vector? v)\n  1385\t                       (throw (ex-info\n  1386\t                                \"Projected :yin.debruijn/operands is not an ordered vector\"\n  1387\t                                {:rule :unsupported-value,\n  1388\t                                 :slot slot,\n  1389\t                                 :value v,\n  1390\t                                 :hash h})))\n  1391\t                     v)\n  1392\t                   [(get record slot)])]\n  1393\t        (doseq [ref refs]\n  1394\t          (when-not (contains? records ref)\n  1395\t            (throw (ex-info \"Projected child hash resolves to no record\"\n  1396\t                            {:rule :dangling-ref, :hash ref, :via h, :slot slot}))))))\n  1397\t    {:fingerprint fingerprint, :records records}))\n  1398\t\n  1399\t\n  1400\t;; =============================================================================\n  1401\t;; D4: the dao.stream forward adapter (§6)\n  1402\t;; =============================================================================\n  1403\t\n  1404\t(def forward-default-options\n  1405\t  \"Defaults for `forward-step`: one read or one write per call, terminal\n  1406\t   gap policy — the same shape `dao.stream.forward` gives its copier.\"\n  1407\t  {:batch-budget 1})\n  1408\t\n  1409\t\n  1410\t(defn forward-initial-state\n  1411\t  \"The state `forward-step` consumes: the input cursor, the current\n  1412\t   graph frame (the §2 accumulation the next :yin/root marker closes),\n  1413\t   and pending projected output. The fact index, scope stack, and\n  1414\t   occurrence memo of §1 live inside the pure per-frame projection —\n  1415\t   the index resets with every frame (§2) — so no step carries them.\"\n  1416\t  [cursor]\n  1417\t  {:cursor cursor, :frame [], :pending []})\n  1418\t\n  1419\t\n  1420\t(defn- forward-budget-ok?\n   445\t   nil, both booleans, a decomposed-NFC string, int, integral and\n   446\t   non-integral doubles, keyword, symbol, vector, set, and map.\n   447\t   Negative zero and lists are NOT here: dao.jing.file's text codec does\n   448\t   not carry them on every host. On CLJS pr-str spells -0.0 as 0, which\n   449\t   the store's print-based address does not notice, so the projected\n   450\t   reader diagnoses :hash-mismatch; on Dart a list literal fails the\n   451\t   store's own codec round-trip check, so the write is refused. Both are\n   452\t   pinned by `values-the-file-codec-cannot-carry-are-refused-not-corrupted`;\n   453\t   lists stay covered in memory by `list-literals-persist-in-memory`.\"\n   454\t  [(app (lam '[x y]\n   455\t             {:type :if,\n   456\t              :test (app (v '<) (v 'x) (lit 1)),\n   457\t              :consequent {:type :stream/put,\n   458\t                           :target {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4},\n   459\t                           :val {:type :stream/next,\n   460\t                                 :source {:type :stream/cursor,\n   461\t                                          :source {:type :stream/close,\n   462\t                                                   :source {:type :vm/store-get,\n   463\t                                                            :key 'k}}}}},\n   464\t              :alternate (app (v 'list)\n   465\t                              {:type :vm/store-put, :key 'k, :val 5}\n   466\t                              {:type :vm/gensym, :prefix \"g\"}\n   467\t                              {:type :vm/current-continuation}\n   468\t                              {:type :vm/park}\n   469\t                              {:type :vm/resume, :parked-id :p1, :val (v 'y)}\n   470\t                              {:type :dao.stream.apply/call,\n   471\t                               :op :op/echo,\n   472\t                               :operands [(lit 1)]}\n   473\t                              {:type :lambda, :macro? true, :params '[m], :body (v 'm)})})\n   474\t        (lit 3))\n   475\t   (app (v 'list)\n   476\t        (lit nil)\n   477\t        (lit true)\n   478\t        (lit false)\n   479\t        (lit \"é\")\n   480\t        (lit 7)\n   481\t        (lit 2.0)\n   482\t        (lit 1.5)\n   483\t        (lit :ns/kw)\n   484\t        (lit 'ns/sym)\n   485\t        (lit [1 \"a\" :k])\n   486\t        (lit #{1 \"b\" :c})\n   487\t        (lit {:a [1 2], \"k\" #{nil}}))])\n   488\t\n   489\t\n   490\t(deftest every-node-type-and-scalar-class-round-trips-through-durable-storage\n   491\t  (let [path (temp-path)]\n   492\t    (try\n   493\t      (let [store (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   494\t            addresses (mapv (fn [ast]\n   495\t                              (get-in (persist! ast (recording-writer) store)\n   496\t                                      [:projected :address]))\n   497\t                            durable-programs)\n   498\t            _ (jing/close! store)\n   499\t            reopened (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   500\t            stored (mapv (fn [address]\n   501\t                           (:yin.debruijn/datoms (jing/get reopened address ::absent)))\n   502\t                         addresses)]\n   503\t        (jing/close! reopened)\n   504\t        (is (every? jing/segment-address? addresses))\n   505\t        (doseq [[ast datoms] (map vector durable-programs stored)]\n   506\t          (is (= (select-keys (debruijn/project-datoms\n   507\t                                (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root ast)))\n   508\t                              [:fingerprint :records])\n   509\t                 (debruijn/datoms->projected datoms))\n   510\t              \"the reopened envelope reads back to the original projection\")))\n   511\t      (finally (cleanup-file path)))))\n   512\t\n   513\t\n   514\t(def ^:private host\n   515\t  ;; :cljd first: the ClojureDart host pass also reads :clj\n   516\t  #?(:cljd :cljd :clj :clj :cljs :cljs))\n   517\t\n   518\t\n   519\t(deftest values-the-file-codec-cannot-carry-are-refused-not-corrupted\n   520\t  ;; one law on every host: a durable round trip is exact, or it is refused\n   521\t  ;; loudly — at write, nothing stored (Dart's list case), or at read as\n   522\t  ;; :hash-mismatch (CLJS's -0.0 case) — never a silent change of value.\n   523\t  ;; No case requires a refusal on any host, so a codec fix cannot break\n   524\t  ;; it; :exact-on names only the hosts already shown to carry the value.\n   525\t  (doseq [{:keys [label ast exact-on]}\n   526\t          [{:label \"negative zero\",\n   527\t            :ast (app (v 'list) (lit -0.0) (lit 0.0)),\n   528\t            :exact-on #{:clj :cljd}}\n   529\t           {:label \"a list of integers\",\n   530\t            :ast (app (v 'list) (lit (list 1 2))),\n   531\t            :exact-on #{:clj}}\n   532\t           {:label \"a list holding a double\",\n   533\t            :ast (app (v 'list) (lit (list 1 2.5))),\n   534\t            :exact-on #{:clj}}]]\n   535\t    (testing label\n   536\t      (let [path (temp-path)]\n   537\t        (try\n   538\t          (let [store (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   539\t                projected (:projected (persist! ast (recording-writer) store))\n   540\t                _ (jing/close! store)\n   541\t                original (select-keys (debruijn/project-datoms\n   542\t                                        (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root ast)))\n   543\t                                      [:fingerprint :records])]\n   544\t            (if (= :ok (:outcome projected))\n   545\t              (let [reopened (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   546\t                    stored (:yin.debruijn/datoms\n   547\t                             (jing/get reopened (:address projected) ::absent))\n   548\t                    _ (jing/close! reopened)\n   549\t                    read-back (try (debruijn/datoms->projected stored)\n   550\t                                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n   551\t                                     (ex-data e)))]\n   552\t                (is (or (= original read-back)\n   553\t                        (contains? #{:hash-mismatch :unsupported-value}\n   554\t                                   (:rule read-back)))\n   555\t                    \"stored: exact, or refused at read as :hash-mismatch or\n   556\t                     :unsupported-value (an integral JS number)\"))\n   557\t              (do (is (= :diagnostic (:outcome projected)))\n   558\t                  (is (= :projected-write-failed (get-in projected [:diagnostic :rule]))\n   559\t                      \"refused at write by the store's own codec check\")\n   560\t                  (is (empty? (jing-file/records path))\n   561\t                      \"nothing was half-written for the refused program\")))\n   562\t            (when (contains? exact-on host)\n   563\t              (is (= :ok (:outcome projected)))\n   564\t              (when (= :ok (:outcome projected))\n   565\t                (is (= original\n   566\t                       (let [reopened (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   567\t                             stored (:yin.debruijn/datoms\n   568\t                                      (jing/get reopened (:address projected) ::absent))]\n   569\t            