{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-23 18:58:44 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-24 01:58:44 +0700 ICT\n\n**APPROVED**\n\n1. **Finding 1 — Resolved.** [`canonical-value-table`](/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-debruijn-type-preservation/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:91) contains no `:javascript` policy. Safe-integer classification resides exclusively in the CLJS-guarded `js-number-class`. The updated descriptor hash passes its pinned fixture.\n\n2. **Finding 2 — Resolved.** The [reader](/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-debruijn-type-preservation/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc:1363) checks ambiguous integral numbers before throwing generic `:hash-mismatch`. Recursive detection covers map keys, values, and collections. Valid hashes still pass; unverifiable records remain rejected. Bare and nested foreign-double fixtures pass.\n\n3. **Finding 3 — Resolved.** The [worktree design document](/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-debruijn-type-preservation/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:196) consistently uses `:dim/contract-version`; the incorrect keyword is absent.\n\nThe [pipeline assertion](/Users/sto/workspace/worktree-debruijn-type-preservation/test/yin/vm/pipeline_test.cljc:552) is architecturally justified. An in-memory reproduction confirmed that the JS text codec converts `-0.0` to `0`, triggering the new ambiguity refusal. Exact-round-trip requirements remain enforced for supported hosts.\n\nContract version remains **1**. The blog no longer claims numeric lossiness by design. Projection remains separate from execution, with no new architectural concerns or P0–P3 findings.\n\nValidation: JVM **79 tests / 358 assertions**; Node **79 tests / 337 assertions**, all passing. Node used existing compiled artifacts, verified to differ only by formatting and an equivalent fixture-binding refactor. Dart and file-writing pipeline tests were not rerun under this read-only review.\n\nNo files edited."}}
